{"c":[{"id":"35936a7e83eb504c","sum":"B29-B30/D2-06: a continued Ask refuses a changed form (ask.ts fieldSeen); page presses are hand-offs; only a digest-named goalAccept runs goal steps (Target.exact); GoalRuns.blocked is null once a segment ends; goal writes skip Cc/Bcc/Subject, To = answered From.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"73cd22e0cad86c6d","sum":"B29/D2-06: a continued Ask refuses a changed form by ask.ts fieldSeen; choice questions go only to askChoices consumers. Page presses are hand-offs; only a goalAccept with its digest runs goal steps, never taskControl; goal targets are Target.exact.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1c75543de1b1c0e8","sum":"B29: a continued Ask refuses a changed form by ask.ts fieldSeen (before and after fill's Jev calls): add to fieldSeen whatever fill starts reading. Questions with choices go only to a consumer whose hello lists askChoices; others read AskRefused's sentence.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2ff420afa6ce639a","text":"B29: a continued Ask refuses a changed form by ask.ts fieldSeen, checked before and after the fill's Jev calls; three reviews each found something fill reads that the record missed, so add to fieldSeen whatever fill starts reading.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092127Z-c755285b7eff0669","text":"B29: Ask questions with choices (planner/choices.ts) go only to a consumer whose hello lists askChoices; AskAsks extends AskRefused, so any other caller reads the old refusal sentence.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cf5de0df55b6d70e","sum":"D2-06: 'Continue' stays unclassified; the one goal press is e:reveal on a whole 'Next'; page presses are hand-offs. Only a goalAccept (goalId, segment, digest) runs goal steps; a goal task is never resumed by taskControl; goal targets are Target.exact.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T105430Z-1712f90f65a11b14","text":"D2-06: 'Continue' is deliberately unclassified at every press boundary (it confirms destructive macOS dialogs); the one goal press capability is e:reveal on a whole 'Next' (goals/capabilities.ts). Page presses are always hand-offs.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T105430Z-1ba2dff3c7f2e7e3","text":"D2-06: only a goalAccept (goalId, segment, digest) runs a goal's steps; a goal task (GoalRuns.owns) is never resumed by taskControl, and a pause stops it. Goal targets are Target.exact (key+role, a button's label): resolveLocally never falls back for them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"046b14781a65d0ff","sum":"D2-06/B30: GoalRuns.blocked must return null once a segment ends, or undo is refused; a goal host's plan Ask comes back as AskGoal. Keep name patterns case-sensitive; goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc/Subject, and To takes only the answered message's From.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"24a976c12b8a54f1","sum":"D2-06/B30: GoalRuns.blocked (inside Helper.authorize) must return null once a segment ends, or undo is refused. A goal host's Ask with route plan comes back as AskGoal (planAsk goals:true) for helper.offerGoal; other consumers keep planTask/planWithCode.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T105431Z-2d9978b4db29946e","text":"D2-06: GoalRuns.blocked runs inside Helper.authorize before every act; it must return null once a segment ends, or a goal task's undo (undoBlocked -> authorize) is refused.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T120548Z-9e86109ce30422ae","text":"B30: a goal-planning host's Ask with route plan is offered as a D2-06 goal (planAsk goals:true returns AskGoal; helper.offerGoal); other consumers keep planTask/planWithCode. planAsk overloads: goals absent/false types as AskDraft.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b7329c13cd423b17","sum":"B30: keep name patterns case-sensitive (the i flag folds \\p{Lu}). Goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc or Subject; To takes only the From of the message the reply answers, rechecked at accept (drafts.ts senderOf); D2-06 scenes need mailWindow line 0 to be From.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T120548Z-b6135cb945f89335","text":"B30: JS regex with the i flag folds \\p{Lu} to match lower case too; a case-insensitive name pattern let 'Thanks, I'll pay' skip Jev. Keep name patterns case-sensitive.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T120548Z-c27c662d572bf540","text":"B30: goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc or Subject, and To takes only the From address in the header block of the message the reply window answers (Re: <subject>), rechecked at accept (drafts.ts senderOf). D2-06 scenes rely on mailWindow line 0 being its From header.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"27eaa3d887b9c175","sum":"B30/R2/R3: drafts.ts checks goal text as whole typed facts (no token allowlists); replayed typing carries its value and focusedKey in one snapshot. Jev: what it judges in state, rules in instructions; R3 evals: fake clock, await a flush.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"08019c2469975896","sum":"B30: drafts.ts checks drafted text as whole typed facts; fix holes with whole-expression rules, never token allowlists. R2: replayed typing carries its typed value in the text's snapshot, with focusedKey; Router 1 is skipped only for consented held-offer records from a host.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"60828e069b1c490e","sum":"B30: drafts.ts checks drafted goal text as whole typed facts (every digit in a fact; a from ref stands for its source); fix holes with whole-expression rules, never token allowlists. R2: replayed typing must carry its typed value in the same snapshot as its text.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T120623Z-4f068d6de508aa09","text":"B30: drafted goal text is checked in goals/drafts.ts as whole typed facts; every digit must land in a fact, and a from value ref stands for its source window or memory. Two reviews found recombination holes: add whole-expression rules, never token allowlists.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T155131Z-2d735fed11dec073","text":"R2: scripts that replay typing must send a typed value (snapshot values) in the same snapshot as its text: a value that arrives after the sentence boundary opens no breakpoint, so the event card is never listed.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9774fe46b42d75d6","sum":"R2: recorded snapshots need the reader's focusedKey or Router 1 abstains (A5's offers-loop.ndjson until 831ab47). Router 1 is skipped only for Helper.consentedCandidates offers on a held offer's own record; messages writing such records count only from a host session.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T155131Z-b3055d198779a6ea","text":"R2: a recorded snapshot without the reader's focusedKey makes Router 1 read 'the cursor is not in a text field' and abstain; A5's offers-loop.ndjson lacked it until 831ab47, which is why H6 saw the loop abstain.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T155145Z-05c6fed3ed39acff","text":"R2: Router 1 is skipped only for offers Helper.consentedCandidates builds on a held offer's own record (routing/consent.ts). Messages that write such records (skillAnswer, resume, skills/ save, watch role) count only from a host session.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"34b44a5905bccdea","sum":"R3: put what Jev judges in state, the rule in instructions; Router 1's task question is its own request. corpus-eval --real-clock skips the cooldown timer (use the fake clock); with jev.holding await a flush, not coord.idle().","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ce9d88d32e0d9097","sum":"R3: corpus-eval --real-clock settle() skips the router cooldown timer, so run incoming-line moments on the fake clock; with jev.holding a stale reply frees the slot and the next call starts at once, so await a flush, not coord.idle().","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-3e0249266797e51f","text":"R3: corpus-eval --real-clock settle() does not wait the router cooldown timer, so an incoming line's later context is never scored; run incoming-line moments on the fake clock.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-4f977dd1bf6c45f7","text":"R3: coordinator tests with jev.holding: a stale reply now frees the slot and the next field's call starts at once, so await a flush, not coord.idle(), while a call is held (idle would wait on the held call).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7d9ef00b5bb5eb15","sum":"R3: Jev judges state against short criteria: put what it judges in state, the rule in instructions (sentence inside the act option split 8/14 vs 14/14). Router 1's task question is its own request after outcome; one shared state moved outcomes (m34 write 0.75 -> 0.32).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-539f47d0a41290db","text":"R3: Jev (System One) judges the request state against short criteria; put what it judges in state and the rule in instructions. Router 1's task question with the sentence inside the act option split ~50/50 (r3 task-wording probe 8/14 vs 14/14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-75585e5911775e88","text":"R3: Router 1's task question (judge.ts) is its own request after the outcome question; with the offer in one shared state the outcome answers moved (corpus m34 write 0.75 -> 0.32).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
